const e="2016-english1",i=2016,t="英语一",a="2016年英语一",o=[{id:"sec-cloze",type:"cloze",title:"英语知识运用",directions:"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)",articles:[{id:"cloze-1",title:"完形填空",type:"cloze",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:"In Cambodia, the choice of a spouse is a complex one for the young male. It may involve not only his parents and his friends, "},{type:"blank",blankId:1},{type:"paragraph",content:" those of the young woman, but also a matchmaker. A young man can "},{type:"blank",blankId:2},{type:"paragraph",content:" a likely spouse on his own and then ask his parents to "},{type:"blank",blankId:3},{type:"paragraph",content:" the marriage negotiations, or the young man's parents may make the choice of a spouse, giving the child little to say in the selection. "},{type:"blank",blankId:4},{type:"paragraph",content:" , a girl may veto the spouse her parents have chosen. "},{type:"blank",blankId:5},{type:"paragraph",content:" a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other to make sure its child is marrying "},{type:"blank",blankId:6},{type:"paragraph",content:" a good family. The traditional wedding is a long and colorful affair. Formerly it lasted three days, "},{type:"blank",blankId:7},{type:"paragraph",content:" by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half. Buddhist priests offer a short sermon and "},{type:"blank",blankId:8},{type:"paragraph",content:" prayers of blessing. Parts of the ceremony involve ritual hair cutting, "},{type:"blank",blankId:9},{type:"paragraph",content:" cotton threads soaked in holy water around the bride's and groom's wrists, and "},{type:"blank",blankId:10},{type:"paragraph",content:" a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples to bless the "},{type:"blank",blankId:11},{type:"paragraph",content:" . Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife's parents and may "},{type:"blank",blankId:12},{type:"paragraph",content:" with them up to a year, "},{type:"blank",blankId:13},{type:"paragraph",content:" they can build a new house nearby. Divorce is legal and easy to "},{type:"blank",blankId:14},{type:"paragraph",content:" , but not common. Divorced persons are "},{type:"blank",blankId:15},{type:"paragraph",content:" with some disapproval. Each spouse retains "},{type:"blank",blankId:16},{type:"paragraph",content:" property he or she "},{type:"blank",blankId:17},{type:"paragraph",content:" into the marriage, and jointly-acquired property is "},{type:"blank",blankId:18},{type:"paragraph",content:" equally. Divorced persons may remarry, but a gender prejudice "},{type:"blank",blankId:19},{type:"paragraph",content:" up: The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry "},{type:"blank",blankId:20},{type:"paragraph",content:" the woman must wait ten months."}]}],questions:[{id:1,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"as well as",B:"by way of",C:"on behalf of",D:"with regard to"},answer:"A",analysis:'as well as 【线索】空处在做"再加上"的并列叠加 线索在本句：It may involve not only his parents and his friends, __(1)__ those of the young woman。前有 not only，空后是 those of the young woman（女方的父母朋 【选项】 A) as well as ✓ 正合"以及"的并列添加 as well as 意为"以及、还有"，把 those of the young woman 添加到前面 his parents and his B) by way of ✗ 义为"经由"，逻辑不符 C) on behalf of ✗ 义为"代表"，逻辑不符 D) with regard to ✗ 义为"关于"，逻辑不符 【验证】代入后 not only his parents and his friends, __(1)__ those of the young woman 读',position:0},{id:2,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"adapt to",B:"provide for",C:"compete with",D:"decide on"},answer:"D",analysis:'decide on 【线索】本句讲年轻人"自己选"配偶 线索在本句：A young man can __(2)__ a likely spouse on his own and then ask his parents to __(3)__ the marriage negotiations。on his own（独自）+ then ask his 【选项】A) adapt to ✗ 义为"适应"，对象不符 B) provide for ✗ 义为"供养"，时机不符 C) compete with ✗ 义为"竞争"，逻辑不符 D) decide on ✓ 义为"选定"，正合择偶 decide on 表"对……做出决定、选定"，decide on a likely spouse on his own 即"自己选定一 个中意的对象"，与下文 then ask his parents 的择偶流程完美衔接。 【验证】代入读作"年轻人可以自己选定一个中意的对象，然后请父母去安排婚事谈判"，decide on a likely spouse on his own 与本段"择偶过程"主线一致。',position:0},{id:3,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"renew",B:"close",C:"arrange",D:"postpone"},answer:"C",analysis:'arrange 【线索】父母被请来"启动"谈判 线索在本句：ask his parents to __(3)__ the marriage negotiations。年轻人选定对象后 【选项】A) renew ✗ 义为"续办"，阶段不符 B) close ✗ 义为"结束"，阶段相反 C) arrange ✓ 义为"安排操办"，正合 arrange 表"安排、操办"，arrange the marriage negotiations 即"操办婚事谈判"，正是父母被 D) postpone ✗ 义为"推迟"，逻辑不符 【验证】代入读作"请父母去操办婚事谈判"，arrange the marriage negotiations 顺承上文 decide',position:0},{id:4,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"In theory",B:"In time",C:"Above all",D:"For example"},answer:"A",analysis:`In theory 【线索】上句父母可包办，本句女孩"可否决" 线索跨句：上文 the young man's parents may make the choice of a spouse, giving the child little to say in the selection（父母可包办、孩子几乎没发言权），本句 a girl may veto the spouse her parents have chosen（女孩可否决）。两句表面矛盾——现实 里没发言权，但"理论上"仍可否决，故需 In theory。 【选项】 A) In theory ✓ "理论上"化解前后张力 B) In time ✗ 义为"最终/及时"，无逻辑 C) Above all ✗ 义为"最重要的是"，递进不符 D) For example ✗ 义为"例如"，本句非举例 【验证】代入读作"理论上，女孩可以否决父母选的配偶"，In theory, a girl may veto the spouse her parents have chosen. 既承认上文的现实约束，又点出名义权利，逻辑自洽。`,position:0},{id:5,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"Although",B:"Lest",C:"After",D:"Unless"},answer:"C",analysis:'After 【线索】"选定后"才"互相调查"，时间先后 线索在本句：__(5)__ a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other to make sure its child is marrying __(6)__ a good family。"配偶已被选定"（完成）与"两家 【选项】A) Although ✗ 义为"虽然"，无让步关系 B) Lest ✗ 义为"以免"，逻辑不符 C) After ✓ 义为"在……之后"，正合时序 After 表"在……之后"，After a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the D) Unless ✗ 义为"除非"，否定条件不符 【验证】代入读作"配偶被选定之后，每家都会调查对方"，After a spouse has been selected 把择',position:0},{id:6,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"within",B:"into",C:"from",D:"through"},answer:"B",analysis:'into 【线索】marry into = 嫁入/娶入好人家 线索在本句：to make sure its child is marrying __(6)__ a good family。两家调查是为 确认孩子"嫁入/娶入"一个好家庭，marry into a family 是固定搭配，表"通过婚姻进入某 家庭"。 【选项】A) within ✗ 义为"在……之内"，搭配错 within 表"在……范围内"，marry within 不表"嫁入"，且"在一个好家庭之内结婚"语义别扭。 B) into ✓ marry into 固定搭配，正合 into 与 marry 构成固定搭配 marry into a family，表"嫁入/娶入某家庭"，marrying into a good family 即"嫁/娶进一个好人家"，搭配与语义双对。 C) from ✗ 义为"来自"，方向相反 from 表"来自"，marry from 不成固定搭配，方向是"从某家出来"，与"进入好家庭"相悖。 D) through ✗ 义为"穿过"，搭配错 through 表"穿过、通过"，marry through 不是固定搭配，也表达不出"进入某家庭"的含义。 【验证】代入读作"确保孩子娶/嫁进了一个好家庭"，marrying into a good family 搭配地道，',position:0},{id:7,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"since",B:"or",C:"so",D:"but"},answer:"D",analysis:'but 【线索】"三天"对"一天半"，时长缩短反差 线索在本句：前 Formerly it lasted three days（过去三天）对后 by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half（80年代缩到一天半）。Formerly 与 by the 1980s 【选项】A) since ✗ 义为"因为/自从"，无因果时间链 B) or ✗ 义为"或者"，非选择关系 C) so ✗ 义为"所以"，无因果 D) but ✓ 义为"但"，正合时长反差 but 表转折，Formerly it lasted three days, but by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a 【验证】代入读作"以前持续三天，但到80年代通常只持续一天半"，Formerly it lasted three days, but by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half 转折顺畅，呼应本段"传统',position:0},{id:8,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"test",B:"recite",C:"copy",D:"create"},answer:"B",analysis:'recite 【线索】僧侣"念诵"祝福祷文 线索在本句：Buddhist priests offer a short sermon and __(8)__ prayers of blessing。 【选项】A) test ✗ 义为"测试"，对象不符 B) recite ✓ 义为"念诵"，正合仪式 recite 表"背诵、念诵"，recite prayers of blessing 即"诵念祝福祷文"，正是僧侣在婚礼上做的 事，与 offer a short sermon 并列自然。 C) copy ✗ 义为"抄写"，动作不符 D) create ✗ 义为"创作"，与传统冲突 【验证】代入读作"僧侣做简短布道并念诵祝福祷文"，recite prayers of blessing 与 offer a short',position:0},{id:9,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"folding",B:"piling",C:"wrapping",D:"tying"},answer:"D",analysis:`tying 【线索】棉线"系"在新人手腕上 线索在本句：__(9)__ cotton threads soaked in holy water around the bride's and groom's wrists。把浸过圣水的棉线 around（环绕）新郎新娘的手腕，常识动作是"系、 缠"，folding（折）、piling（堆）都无法与 around the wrists 搭配。 【选项】A) folding ✗ 义为"折叠"，无法环绕 folding 表"折叠"，棉线无法"折在手腕周围"，与 around the wrists 不搭。 B) piling ✗ 义为"堆叠"，动作不符 C) wrapping ✗ 义近"缠绕"，但不及 tying 准 wrapping 表"包裹、缠绕"，方向接近，但与细棉线（threads）系在手腕的仪式相比，wrap 更 D) tying ✓ 义为"系、绑"，正合仪式 tying 表"系、绑"，tying cotton threads ... around the bride's and groom's wrists 即"把棉线 【验证】代入读作"把浸过圣水的棉线系在新郎新娘的手腕上"，tying cotton threads soaked in holy water around the bride's and groom's wrists 描述祝福仪式细节，与本段并列的 hair cutting、passing a candle 同属仪式动作，全局自洽。`,position:0},{id:10,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"passing",B:"lighting",C:"hiding",D:"serving"},answer:"A",analysis:'passing 【线索】蜡烛在一圈夫妇间"传递" 线索在本句：__(10)__ a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples to bless the __(11)__。蜡烛 around a circle of couples（绕着一圈夫妇），并 to bless（祝福新人），常识动作是"传递"蜡烛，lighting/hiding/serving 都无法与"绕圈 【选项】 A) passing ✓ 义为"传递"，正合绕圈祝福 passing 表"传递"，passing a candle around a circle of happily married and respected B) lighting ✗ 义为"点燃"，与绕圈不符 lighting 表"点燃"，"点燃一支蜡烛绕一圈夫妇"逻辑断裂，around a circle 体现的是传递而非 C) hiding ✗ 义为"藏"，与祝福相悖 hiding 表"藏"，藏蜡烛无法"祝福新人"，与 to bless 目的冲突。 D) serving ✗ 义为"端上"，对象不符 【验证】代入读作"把蜡烛在一圈幸福受敬重的夫妇间传递以祝福新人"，passing a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples to bless the union 与同段其他仪式动',position:0},{id:11,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"association",B:"meeting",C:"collection",D:"union"},answer:"D",analysis:'union 【线索】祝福的对象是新人的"结合"（婚姻） 线索跨句承接：上文 to bless the __(11)__ 紧承 newlyweds 的婚礼仪式，被祝福的应是"这 桩婚姻、这对新人的结合"。union 一词常指"婚姻结合"（marriage union），最贴婚礼 【选项】A) association ✗ 义偏"协会/关联"，不专指婚姻 B) meeting ✗ 义为"会面"，程度太轻 C) collection ✗ 义为"收集物"，对象不符 collection 表"收藏、集合（物品）"，与"祝福新人结合"风马牛不相及。 D) union ✓ 义为"结合（婚姻）"，正合 union 常指"结合，尤指婚姻"，to bless the union 即"祝福这桩婚姻结合"，最贴婚礼祝福语 【验证】代入读作"传烛祝福这对新人的结合（婚姻）"，to bless the union 收束整段婚礼仪式描',position:0},{id:12,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"grow",B:"part",C:"live",D:"deal"},answer:"C",analysis:`live 【线索】新人搬去岳父母家，与其"同住"一年 线索在本句：Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife's parents and may __(12)__ with them up to a year。前句 move in with the wife's parents（搬进女方父母 【选项】A) grow ✗ 义为"成长"，搭配不符 grow 表"成长"，grow with them 不表"同住"，与 move in 语境不接。 B) part ✗ 义为"分开"，逻辑相反 part 表"分开"，part with them 是"与他们分离"，与刚搬进同住正好相反。 C) live ✓ 义为"居住"，正合同住 live 表"居住"，live with them up to a year 即"和他们同住长达一年"，顺承 move in，描述新 D) deal ✗ 义为"处理/打交道"，语义不符 【验证】代入读作"新人传统上搬进女方父母家，可能和他们同住长达一年"，live with them up to a year 顺承 move in、引出下句 build a new house，居住主线连贯。`,position:0},{id:13,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"whereas",B:"until",C:"for",D:"if"},answer:"B",analysis:'until 【线索】同住"直到"盖好新房 线索在本句：may live with them up to a year, __(13)__ they can build a new house 填 until（直到）。 【选项】A) whereas ✗ 义为"然而"，无对比 B) until ✓ 义为"直到"，正合时间界限 until 表"直到"，live with them up to a year, until they can build a new house nearby 即"同 C) for ✗ 义为"因为"，因果不成立 D) if ✗ 义为"如果"，条件不符 【验证】代入读作"可能和他们同住约一年，直到能在附近盖起新房"，until they can build a new house nearby 把"同住"自然过渡到"独立成家"，时间链清楚。',position:0},{id:14,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"follow",B:"obtain",C:"challenge",D:"avoid"},answer:"B",analysis:'obtain 【线索】离婚"合法且易于办得" 线索在本句：Divorce is legal and easy to __(14)__, but not common.。legal（合法）与 空并列，描述离婚"既合法又易于___"，自然语义是"易于办得/获得"，obtain a divorce（办 【选项】A) follow ✗ 义为"遵循"，搭配不符 follow 表"遵循、跟随"，"离婚易于遵循"语义不通，follow a divorce 不成立。 B) obtain ✓ 义为"获得/办得"，正合 obtain 表"获得、取得"，easy to obtain 即"易于办成（离婚）"，obtain a divorce 是地道搭 C) challenge ✗ 义为"质疑"，逻辑不符 challenge 表"质疑、挑战"，"离婚易于质疑"与"合法"并列读不通。 D) avoid ✗ 义为"避免"，方向相反 【验证】代入读作"离婚合法且易于办成，但并不常见"，Divorce is legal and easy to obtain, but',position:0},{id:15,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"isolated",B:"persuaded",C:"viewed",D:"exposed"},answer:"C",analysis:'viewed 【线索】离婚者"被以非议眼光看待" 线索在本句：Divorced persons are __(15)__ with some disapproval.。with some disapproval（带着些许反对/非议）是看待的态度，be viewed with disapproval（被以非 【选项】A) isolated ✗ 义为"被孤立"，搭配不符 isolated 表"被孤立"，isolated with disapproval 不成搭配，with disapproval 是看待态度而非孤 B) persuaded ✗ 义为"被劝说"，逻辑不符 C) viewed ✓ 义为"被看待"，正合态度框架 viewed 表"看待"，viewed with some disapproval 即"被以些许非议的眼光看待"，be viewed D) exposed ✗ 义为"被暴露"，搭配不符 exposed 表"暴露于"，常接 to，exposed with disapproval 不成立。 【验证】代入读作"离婚者会被以些许非议的眼光看待"，Divorced persons are viewed with some disapproval. 紧承 not common，点明社会态度，全局自洽。',position:0},{id:16,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"whatever",B:"however",C:"whenever",D:"wherever"},answer:"A",analysis:'whatever 【线索】空后紧跟名词 property，需限定词 线索在本句结构：retains __(16)__ property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage。空要 定词修饰 property。 【选项】 A) whatever ✓ 可作限定词修饰名词，正合 whatever 表"无论什么的、任何"，可直接修饰名词 property，whatever property he or she brought into the marriage 即"各自带入婚姻的任何财产"，语法语义双对。 B) however ✗ 副词性，不能修饰名词 however 表"无论如何"，修饰形容词/副词，不能直接接名词 property，语法不通。 C) whenever ✗ 表时间，词性不符 whenever 表"无论何时"，是时间副词从句引导词，不能修饰名词 property。 D) wherever ✗ 表地点，词性不符 wherever 表"无论何地"，是地点副词从句引导词，无法修饰名词 property。 【验证】代入读作"各自保留他或她带入婚姻的任何财产"，Each spouse retains whatever property he or she brought into the marriage 语法成立，与下文"共同财产均分"对照，',position:0},{id:17,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"changed",B:"brought",C:"shaped",D:"pushed"},answer:"B",analysis:'brought 【线索】各自婚前"带入"婚姻的财产 线索在本句：whatever property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage。与 into the marriage 搭配、表"把（婚前的）财产带进婚姻"的动词是 bring，bring sth into the marriage 是地道说法。 【选项】A) changed ✗ 义为"改变"，搭配不符 changed 表"改变"，change property into the marriage 不成立，方向短语不搭。 B) brought ✓ 义为"带入"，正合 brought 表"带来、带入"，property he or she brought into the marriage 即"他或她带入婚姻 的财产"，bring sth into the marriage 是地道搭配，准确表"婚前财产带进婚姻"。 C) shaped ✗ 义为"塑造"，语义不符 D) pushed ✗ 义为"推"，搭配生硬 pushed 表"推"，push property into the marriage 搭配生硬、不地道，不表"带入"的自然含义。 【验证】代入读作"各自保留他或她带入婚姻的财产"，whatever property he or she brought into',position:0},{id:18,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"withdrawn",B:"invested",C:"donated",D:"divided"},answer:"D",analysis:'divided 【线索】共同财产被"均分" 线索在本句：jointly-acquired property is __(18)__ equally，并与上句 Each spouse retains whatever property he or she brought into the marriage 对照——各自婚前财产 各自留，共同财产则 equally（平等地）处置，divided equally（平均分配）最合离婚财产 【选项】A) withdrawn ✗ 义为"撤回"，与 equally 不符 withdrawn 表"撤回、取走"，withdrawn equally 不合"离婚分财产"语境，撤回不涉及"平分"。 B) invested ✗ 义为"投资"，语境不符 C) donated ✗ 义为"捐赠"，语境不符 D) divided ✓ 义为"分割"，正合均分 divided 表"分割、分配"，jointly-acquired property is divided equally 即"共同财产被平均分 【验证】代入读作"共同获得的财产则平均分配"，jointly-acquired property is divided equally 与',position:0},{id:19,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"clears",B:"shows",C:"warms",D:"breaks"},answer:"B",analysis:`shows 【线索】性别偏见"显露出来"，冒号后举证 线索在本句及冒号后：a gender prejudice __(19)__ up: The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry __(20)__ the woman must wait ten months.。 【选项】A) clears ✗ clear up=澄清/放晴，方向相反 clears 与 up 构成 clear up（消除、澄清、转晴），意为偏见"消失"，与冒号后"偏见确实存在"的 B) shows ✓ show up=显露，正合举证 shows 与 up 构成 show up（显现、暴露出来），a gender prejudice shows up 即"一种性别 C) warms ✗ warm up=变暖/热身，语义不符 warms 与 up 构成 warm up（变暖、热身），与"偏见"主语搭配不通。 D) breaks ✗ break up=破裂/分手，语义不符 breaks 与 up 构成 break up（破裂、解散、分手），"偏见破裂"语义不通，且与举证方向不合。 【验证】代入读作"一种性别偏见显露出来：离婚男性再婚无需等待期，而女性须等十个月"，a gender prejudice shows up 后接冒号例证，先总（偏见显现）后分（具体差别），逻辑`,position:0},{id:20,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"while",B:"once",C:"so that",D:"in that"},answer:"A",analysis:`while 【线索】男性无等待期，"而"女性须等十月 线索在本句：前 The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period（男性无等待期）对 后 the woman must wait ten months（女性须等十个月）。男女待遇相反，正是上文 gender prejudice 的体现，需对比连词 while（而、然而）。 【选项】 A) while ✓ 义为"而"，正合男女对比 while 在此表"而、然而"，The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry while the woman must wait ten months. 把男性无需等待与女性须等十月对照起来， 恰好印证 gender prejudice，对比关系明确。 B) once ✗ 义为"一旦"，时间条件不符 C) so that ✗ 义为"以便"，目的因果不符 D) in that ✗ 义为"因为"，因果不符 【验证】代入读作"离婚男性再婚前没有等待期，而女性必须等十个月"，while the woman must wait ten months 把男女待遇对照鲜明，正是前句 gender prejudice 的落地，收束全文。 OVERVIEW · 通读建境 篇即点出话题：In Cambodia, the choice of a spouse is a complex one for the young male.，由此展开。 择偶（P1）→婚礼仪式（P2）→离婚（P3）三段式时间线 第一段讲选配偶的复杂过程：the choice of a spouse is a complex one；第二段讲传统婚 礼：The traditional wedding is a long and colorful affair.；第三段讲离婚：Divorce is legal and easy to __(14)__, but not common.。三段各自独立、按婚姻生命周期推进，逐空线索 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 2 After a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other to make sure its child is marrying into a good family. Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife's parents and may live with them up to a year, until they can build a new house nearby. HIGH-FREQUENCY · 真题高频词 22 spouse B2 involve B1 n. 配偶 v. 包含 本篇6 次 · 真题 8 句 本篇2 次 · 真题 61 句 property B1 male A2 n. 财产 adj. 男性的 本篇2 次 · 真题 11 句 本篇2 次 · 真题 10 句 view A2 likely A2 n. 观点，看法 adj. 很可能的 本篇1 次 · 真题 91 句 本篇1 次 · 真题 89 句 legal B1 theory B1 adj. 法律的 n. 理论 本篇1 次 · 真题 44 句 本篇1 次 · 真题 39 句 complex B2 un...`,position:0}]},{id:"sec-reading",type:"reading",title:"阅读理解",directions:"Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (40 points)",articles:[{id:"text-1",title:"Text 1",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women. Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. The parliament also agreed to ban websites that "incite excessive thinness" by promoting extreme dieting. Such measures have a couple of uplifting motives. They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health. That's a start. And the ban on ultra-thin models seems to go beyond protecting models from starving themselves to death – as some have done. It tells the fashion industry that it must take responsibility for the signal it sends women, especially teenage girls, about the social tape-measure they must use to determine their individual worth. The bans, if fully enforced, would suggest to women (and many men) that they should not let others be arbiters of their beauty. And perhaps faintly, they hint that people should look to intangible qualities like character and intellect rather than dieting their way to size zero or wasp-waist physiques. The French measures, however, rely too much on severe punishment to change a culture that still regards beauty as skin-deep – and bone-showing. Under the law, using a fashion model that does not meet a government-defined index of body mass could result in a $85,000 fine and six months in prison. The fashion industry knows it has an inherent problem in focusing on material adornment and idealized body types. In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement. In contrast to France's actions, Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models. The newly revised Danish Fashion Ethical Charter clearly states: "We are aware of and take responsibility for the impact the fashion industry has on body ideals, especially on young people." The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute. But in general it relies on a name-and-shame method of compliance. Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step. Even better would be to help elevate notions of beauty beyond the material standards of a particular industry.`}]},{id:"text-2",title:"Text 2",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`For the first time in history more people live in towns than in the country. In Britain this has had a curious result. While polls show Britons rate "the countryside" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support. A century ago Octavia Hill launched the National Trust not to rescue stylish houses but to save "the beauty of natural places for everyone forever." It was specifically to provide city dwellers with spaces for leisure where they could experience "a refreshing air." Hill's pressure later led to the creation of national parks and green belts. They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it. It needs constant guardianship. At the next election none of the big parties seem likely to endorse this sentiment. The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising "off-plan" building where local people might object. The concept of sustainable development has been defined as profitable. Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development. The Liberal Democrats are silent. Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land. Its Campaign to Protect Rural England struck terror into many local Conservative parties. The sensible place to build new houses, factories and offices is where people are, in cities and towns where infrastructure is in place. The London agents Stirling Ackroyd recently identified enough sites for half a million houses in the London area alone, with no intrusion on green belt. What is true of London is even truer of the provinces. The idea that "housing crisis" equals "concreted meadows" is pure lobby talk. The issue is not the need for more houses but, as always, where to put them. Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal. He favours out-of-town shopping sites against high streets. This is not a free market but a biased one. Rural towns and villages have grown and will always grow. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. We do not ruin urban conservation areas. Why ruin rural ones? Development should be planned, not let rip. After the Netherlands, Britain is Europe's most crowded country. Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence, while still permitting low-density urban living. There is no doubt of the alternative – the corrupted landscapes of southern Portugal, Spain or Ireland. Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the political spectrum.`}]},{id:"text-3",title:"Text 3",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`"There is one and only one social responsibility of business," wrote Milton Friedman, a Nobel prize-winning economist, "That is, to use its resources and engage in activities designed to increase its profits." But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut. New research suggests that CSR may create monetary value for companies – at least when they are prosecuted for corruption. The largest firms in America and Britain together spend more than $15 billion a year on CSR, according to an estimate by EPG, a consulting firm. This could add value to their businesses in three ways. First, consumers may take CSR spending as a "signal" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. And third, through a more diffuse "halo effect," whereby its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers and others. Previous studies on CSR have had trouble differentiating these effects because consumers can be affected by all three. A recent study attempts to separate them by looking at bribery prosecutions under America's Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (FCPA). It argues that since prosecutors do not consume a company's products as part of their investigations, they could be influenced only by the halo effect. The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties. Their analysis ruled out the possibility that it was firms' political influence, rather than their CSR stand, that accounted for the leniency: Companies that contributed more to political campaigns did not receive lower fines. In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR. "We estimate that either eliminating a substantial labour- rights concern, such as child labour, or increasing corporate giving by about 20% results in fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment for bribing foreign officials," says one researcher. Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR. Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies. But at least they have demonstrated that when companies get into trouble with the law, evidence of good character can win them a less costly punishment.`}]},{id:"text-4",title:"Text 4",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`There will eventually come a day when The New York Times ceases to publish stories on newsprint. Exactly when that day will be is a matter of debate. "Sometime in the future," the paper's publisher said back in`}]}],questions:[{id:21,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France?",options:{A:"Physical beauty would be redefined.",B:"New runways would be constructed.",C:"Websites about dieting would thrive.",D:"The fashion industry would decline."},answer:"A",analysis:'【判型】According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France? 问的是限定段落里发 【拆句】According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France? 句首 According to 【定位】P1 Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. The parliament also agreed to ban websites that "incite excessive thinness" by promoting extreme dieting. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women ↔ Physical beauty would be redefined 束，Physical beauty would be redefined 是这一结果的最自然概括。 原文 on runways 只是 "走秀的 T 台"，与新建跑道无关；New runways would be constructed 把 runways 误读成机场/赛道层面的 "新建跑道"。 dieting would thrive 反向预测它们将兴旺。 第一段只字未提时尚产业会因此 "衰退"；The fashion industry would decline 是凭空',position:0},{id:22,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:'The phrase "impinging on" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to____',options:{A:"indicating the state of.",B:"heightening the value of.",C:"losing faith in.",D:"doing harm to."},answer:"D",analysis:'短语"impinging on"(第2段第2行)的意思最接近____ A) 表明……的状态。 B) 提高……的价值。 C) 对……失去信心。 D) 对……造成伤害。 【判型】The phrase "impinging on" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to 直接要求选与某短 【拆句】The phrase "impinging on" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to 是一句结构平铺 的陈述句作题干，主语是被引短语，谓语 is closest in meaning to 后接选项作宾语。无 【定位】P2 They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health. 【选项】A) 答非所问 indicating the state of 表 "表明...的状态"，是中性描述，与原文负面语义不符。 heightening the value of 表 "提升...的价值"，是积极动作，与上下文负面极性相反。 losing faith in 意为 "对...失去信心"，主语应是人，而原文主语 looks 是 "外貌"，搭配 D) ✓ 正确 looks that end up impinging on health ↔ doing harm to 上下文 end up 与 starving themselves to death 一同框定 impinging on 必带负面后 果，doing harm to 与之对齐。',position:0},{id:23,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following is true of the fashion industry?",options:{A:"The French measures have already failed.",B:"Its inherent problems are getting worse.",C:"Models are no longer under peer pressure.",D:"New standards are being set in Denmark."},answer:"D",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following is true of the fashion industry? 让考生在四项陈述里选与原文相 【拆句】Which of the following is true of the fashion industry? which 引导的特殊疑问句，is true of 后接对象。结构简单，无陷阱。 【定位】P5 In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement. 【选项】A) 无中生有 原文只对法国措施提出批评 rely too much on severe punishment，但从未说 French measures have already failed——"已经失败" 是凭空升级。 原文 The fashion industry knows it has an inherent problem 只说 "行业意识到固有 问题"，并未声称问题在 getting worse。 原文 rely more on peer pressure for enforcement 明示 "更依赖同行压力"，Models are no longer under peer pressure 正好相反。 D) ✓ 正确 In Denmark ... it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images ↔ New standards are being set in Denmark Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions ↔ New standards are being set in Denmark 第 5、6 段连续两次描述丹麦正在/刚刚订立新标准与新章程，与 New standards are being set in Denmark 一一对应。`,position:0},{id:24,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____",options:{A:"pursuing perfect physical conditions.",B:"caring too much about models' character.",C:"showing little concern for health factors.",D:"setting a high age threshold for models."},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____ 问 "因什么原因被拒"，对应原 【拆句】A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____ 是含空位的陈述句，主语 A designer，谓语 is most likely to be rejected 为情态+被动语态，by CFW 表施动者，for 【定位】P6 Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models. ... The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute. 周（CFW）。 【选项】A) 偷换概念 章程意在反对 idealized body types；追求 perfect physical conditions 恰是章程要纠 perfect physical conditions 可被中性甚至褒义理解，与 CFW 拒绝标准方向有偏差， 原文 character 出现在评论作者立场处，不属于 CFW 拒入条件；而 caring too much about models' character 是 "过度关注品格"，原文从未提此为问题。 C) ✓ 正确 rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models ↔ showing little concern for health factors 章程规定 health 是核心规制对象，违反者被 deny access；故 showing little concern for health factors 正是被 CFW 拒之门外的合理原因。 章程关心模特 age（年龄）是要防止 "年龄过低"，setting a high age threshold for 被 CFW 拒；选项把 "违章" 与 "守章" 倒置。`,position:0},{id:25,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following may be the best title of the text?",options:{A:"The Great Threats to the Fashion Industry",B:"Just Another Round of Struggle for Beauty",C:"A Dilemma for the Starving Models in France",D:"A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals"},answer:"D",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following may be the best title of the text? 直接问最佳标题，要求覆盖全 【拆句】Which of the following may be the best title of the text? which 引导的特殊疑问句，情 态 may 表 "可能" 弱化语气，of the text 限定 title 的范围是 "本文整篇"。无陷阱。 【选项】A) 过度推断 Just Another Round of Struggle for Beauty 把全文降格为 "又一次美的较量"，既未点 出 "时尚业" 与 "体型理想"，又用 Just Another 贬抑作者立场的严肃性。 A Dilemma for the Starving Models in France 只截取第 2 段 starving themselves D) ✓ 正确 focusing on material adornment and idealized body types ↔ A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step ↔ A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals 同时覆盖法国立法、丹麦章程与 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 10 France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women. Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health. It tells the fashion industry that it must take responsibility for the signal it sends women, especially teenage girls, about the social tape-measure they must use to determine their individual worth. 本句成分丰富且包含多个易错点:双宾语结构("tells the fashion industry that..."),定语从句关系代词 省略(两处),同位语("especially teenage girls"),目的状语("to determine..."),以及 "responsibility for" And ...`,position:0},{id:26,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"Britain's public sentiment about the countryside____",options:{A:"is not well reflected in politics.",B:"is fully backed by the royal family.",C:"didn't start till the Shakespearean age.",D:"has brought much benefit to the NHS."},answer:"A",analysis:`【判型】Q26 是不完整陈述句，由选项补全；问的是 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside 的某个客观事实状态，不带 infer/imply 这类信号词。 【拆句】题干 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside 由选项补全为完整陈述句，主语 是 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside，谓语由各选项提供；结构平铺直 【定位】P1 While polls show Britons rate "the countryside" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 this has limited political support ↔ is not well reflected in politics 预判"公众情感缺政治回应"恰与 is not well reflected in politics 一一对应，无需借助他 fully backed by the royal family 凭空升级为"完全支持"。 start till the Shakespearean age 强行赋予时间起源。 NHS 同样只是骄傲对象之一，原文未谈乡村情感"使 NHS 受益"；has brought much benefit to the NHS 偷换关系。`,position:0},{id:27,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"According to Paragraph 2, the achievements of the National Trust are now being____",options:{A:"largely overshadowed.",B:"properly protected.",C:"effectively reinforced.",D:"gradually destroyed."},answer:"D",analysis:`根据第2段,National Trust的成就现在正在被____ 【判型】题干 According to Paragraph 2 是细节题的典型句式，要求按段内事实补完 the achievements of the National Trust are now being。 【拆句】the achievements of the National Trust are now being 用 are being + 过去分词的现在 进行被动语态，强调 achievements 当下正在被怎么对待；考生若忽略 now being（正在 【定位】P2 They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it. It needs constant guardianship. 【选项】A) 偷换概念 原文谈的是"被混凝土物理蚕食"，与 largely overshadowed（在很大程度上被遮蔽/掩 properly protected 是正向"得到妥善保护"，与原文 It needs constant guardianship effectively reinforced 是正向"得到有效强化"，与原文"成就正被吞噬"完全反向。 D) ✓ 正确 concrete consumes more of it ↔ gradually destroyed 预判"成就正被吞噬"恰对应 gradually destroyed——两者同为负向破坏义动词，且时 间副词 every year 与 gradually 在过程描述上等值。`,position:0},{id:28,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3?",options:{A:"Labour is under attack for opposing development.",B:'The Conservatives may abandon "off-plan" building.',C:"Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation.",D:"The Liberal Democrats are losing political influence."},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3? 用 can be inferred 明确要 【拆句】Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3? 是 Which 引导的特殊疑问 句，谓语 can be inferred 为情态被动，强调"能被合理推出"；结构清晰，无陷阱。 【定位】P3 Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land. Its Campaign to Protect Rural England struck terror into many local Conservative parties. 【选项】A) 张冠李戴 原文说 Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development——是 Labour 想架空地方反对开发的规划权，并未说 Labour 原文 The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising "off-plan" building 表明保守党正在推 进 off-plan，而非要放弃。 C) ✓ 正确 Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land ↔ Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation struck terror into many local Conservative parties ↔ Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation Only 排除他党、sensing its chance 暗示机会、struck terror 反映对手警觉——三重 信号共同支持 Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation。 原文仅说 The Liberal Democrats are silent（保持沉默），未给任何关于"政治影响力 下滑"的信息，silent 不等于 losing influence。`,position:0},{id:29,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"The author holds that George Osborne's preference____",options:{A:"shows his disregard for the character of rural areas.",B:"stresses the necessity of easing the housing crisis.",C:"highlights his firm stand against lobby pressure.",D:"reveals a strong prejudice against urban areas."},answer:"A",analysis:`作者认为George Osborne的偏好____ 【判型】题干 The author holds that 要求总结作者对 George Osborne's preference 的判断，需 【拆句】The author holds that George Osborne's preference 是 that 宾语从句作 holds 的宾 语，从句主语 preference 由选项补出谓语；考生易把"preference"误读为"偏爱乡村"，需 结合下文 against 结构辨方向。 【定位】P5 Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal. He favours out-of-town shopping sites against high streets. This is not a free market but a biased one. Rural towns and villages have grown and will always grow. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. We do not ruin urban conservation areas. Why ruin rural ones? 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 building sticks to their edges and respects their character ↔ shows his disregard for the character of rural areas Why ruin rural ones? ↔ shows his disregard for the character of rural areas 预判"Osborne 罔顾乡村风貌"恰与 shows his disregard for the character of rural areas 精准吻合：character 同词复现，respects/disregard 反义对调。 that "housing crisis" equals "concreted meadows" is pure lobby talk. 已把"住房危 原文明说 Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours...——Osborne 正是顺从 场，不是 Osborne 立场。`,position:0},{id:30,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"In the last paragraph, the author shows his appreciation of____",options:{A:"the size of population in Britain.",B:"the enviable urban lifestyle in Britain.",C:"the town-and-country planning in Britain.",D:"the political life in today's Britain."},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】the author shows his appreciation of 直接问作者赞赏的对象，是典型态度题。 【拆句】In the last paragraph, the author shows his appreciation of 主句为 the author shows appreciation，of 后由选项补宾语；语法平铺，无陷阱。 【选项】A) 偷换概念 原文 Britain is Europe's most crowded country 只是引出"为何需要规划"的背景压 low-density urban living 是 town and country planning 的结果之一，while still permitting low-density urban living 中 while still permitting 只表附带保留，作者赞 C) ✓ 正确 Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence ↔ the town-and-country planning in Britain 末段 enviable 的修饰链向上回溯到 town and country planning 这一主语，与 appreciation 在态度极性与对象上完全一致。 Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the 然 ≠ 实然。 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 7 A century ago Octavia Hill launched the National Trust not to rescue stylish houses but to save "the beauty of natural places for everyone forever." It was specifically to provide city dwellers with spaces for leisure where they could experience "a refreshing air." Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development. 句式。where 引导定语从句修饰抽象地点名词(如 planning、situation 等)也是典型用法,学习后可迁 This is not a free market but a biased one. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. There is no doubt of the alternative – the corrupted landscapes of southern Portugal, Spain or Ireland. Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the political spectrum. 主语是动名词短语且含并列结构（"Avo...`,position:0},{id:31,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"The author views Milton Friedman's statement about CSR with____",options:{A:"tolerance.",B:"skepticism.",C:"approval.",D:"uncertainty."},answer:"B",analysis:`A) 宽容 B) 怀疑 C) 赞同 D) 不确定 【判型】The author views Milton Friedman's statement about CSR with____ 的结构是 view sth 【拆句】句子主干是 The author views Milton Friedman's statement ... with____，view A with B 【定位】P1 But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut. 【选项】A) 偷换概念 Friedman 的极端论断，是在"质疑"，而非"容忍"。 B) ✓ 正确 things may not be absolutely clear-cut ↔ skepticism But even if you accept Friedman's premise ↔ skepticism 预判到"温和怀疑"后，四个选项里 tolerance（容忍、偏中）、approval（赞同，正）、 uncertainty（不确定，无方向）都不带"质疑"指向，只有 skepticism 精准命中弱负的`,position:0},{id:32,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"According to Paragraph 2, CSR helps a company by____",options:{A:"guarding it against malpractices.",B:"protecting it from being defamed.",C:"winning trust from consumers.",D:"raising the quality of its products."},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】According to Paragraph 2, CSR helps a company by____ 是 according to + 段号 + 直 【拆句】by + Ving 结构提示空格处是动名词短语，描述 CSR 帮助公司的"方式"。结构简单。 【定位】P2 First, consumers may take CSR spending as a "signal" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. And third, through a more diffuse "halo effect," whereby its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers and others. 【选项】A) 无中生有 guarding it against malpractices 指"保护公司免于不当行为"；第二段三条机制全在 protecting it from being defamed 指"防止公司被诽谤"；第二段没有 defame / reputation damage 这一话题，三条机制谈的都是"为公司挣加分"而非"防止减分"。 C) ✓ 正确 its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers ↔ winning trust from consumers consumers may take CSR spending as a "signal" that a company's products are of high quality ↔ winning trust from consumers consumers 的核心语义。 raising the quality of its products 指"提高产品质量"；但原文是 consumers may take CSR spending as a "signal" that a company's products are of high quality`,position:0},{id:33,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:'The expression "more lenient" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to____',options:{A:"less controversial.",B:"more effective.",C:"more lasting.",D:"less severe."},answer:"D",analysis:'第4段中"more lenient"这一表达在意思上最接近于 【判型】The expression "more lenient" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to____ 是经典的词义题 【拆句】is closest in meaning to 是固定搭配，意为"在含义上最接近"。结构平铺直叙。 【定位】P4 The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties. 【选项】A) 无中生有 more effective 指"更有效的"；把它代入"more effective penalties"是"更有效的处 more lasting 指"更持久的"；lenient 谈的是处罚"强度"，与"持续时间"是两个维度。 D) ✓ 正确 more lenient penalties ↔ less severe fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment ↔ less severe 预判到"处罚更轻"后，把 lenient 与每个选项试代：only less severe 在搭配 penalties',position:0},{id:34,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"When prosecutors evaluate a case, a company's CSR record____",options:{A:"has an impact on their decision.",B:"comes across as reliable evidence.",C:"increases the chance of being penalized.",D:"constitutes part of the investigation."},answer:"A",analysis:`【判型】When prosecutors evaluate a case, a company's CSR record____ 是补全陈述句，直接 问发生了什么，无 infer/imply。 【拆句】When 引导时间状语从句，主句空缺谓语与宾语；空格处要填一个完整的谓语短语来描述 【定位】P5 In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR ↔ has an impact on their decision 预判到"CSR 记录会影响判定"后，选项 has an impact on their decision 用主动语态 +名词化（impact）精确对应原文的被动+动词（influenced）。 comes across as reliable evidence 指"被视为可靠证据"；原文只说 CSR 记录"影响"了 increases the chance of being penalized 指"增加被处罚的概率"；原文恰好相反—— CSR 记录好的公司 tended to get more lenient penalties，处罚反而更轻。 constitutes part of the investigation 指"构成调查的一部分"；原文是检察官"被 CSR`,position:0},{id:35,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following is true of CSR, according to the last paragraph?",options:{A:"Its negative effects on businesses are often overlooked.",B:"The necessary amount of companies' spending on it is unknown.",C:"Companies' financial capacity for it has been overestimated.",D:"It has brought much benefit to the banking industry."},answer:"B",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following is true of CSR, according to the last paragraph 同时限定话题 【拆句】Which of the following is true of X, according to Y? 是判断题的固定句式；主句的真正 主语是 Which (= 哪一项)，of CSR 是限定 true 的范围。结构简单。 【定位】P6 Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR. 【选项】A) 无中生有 Its negative effects on businesses are often overlooked 指"CSR 对企业的负面效应 B) ✓ 正确 does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR ↔ The necessary amount of companies' spending on it is unknown. amount + unknown），匹配度最高。 Companies' financial capacity for it has been overestimated 指"企业为 CSR 投入 It has brought much benefit to the banking industry 指"CSR 给银行业带来了很多 好处"；原文 how much companies are banking on the halo effect 中 banking on 是固定短语"指望、押宝"的意思，与"banking industry（银行业）"毫无关系。 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 11 "There is one and only one social responsibility of business," wrote Milton Friedman, a Nobel prize-winning economist, "That is, to use its resources and engage in activities designed to increase its profits." But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut. First, consumers may take CSR spending as a "signal" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. Previous studies on CSR have had trouble ...`,position:0},{id:36,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to____",options:{A:"the high cost of operation.",B:"the increasing online ad sales.",C:"the pressure from its investors.",D:"the complaints from its readers."},answer:"A",analysis:"【判型】The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to 是一个待补 【拆句】The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to____ 是“主语 + 谓语 (is considering) + 动名词宾语 (ending its print edition) + 状语 (partly due to 【定位】P2 The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper—printing presses, delivery trucks —isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper—printing presses, delivery trucks— isn't just expensive ↔ the high cost of operation 预判得到“制作纸版的开支高且过剩”，选项 the high cost of operation 是对其最直接 的上位归纳，与原文 expensive、excessive 等关键词同义对应。 原文只说 print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts 与 revenue from print is still declining，强调纸广告仍远大于线上广告且纸广告收入在下 滑，根本没有提线上广告销售额在“增长”，选项 the increasing online ad sales 是凭空 从未提及任何来自投资人/股东的压力，the pressure from its investors 在原文里完全 原文 you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you 是",position:0},{id:37,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____",options:{A:"end the print edition for good.",B:"make strategic adjustments.",C:"seek new sources of readership.",D:"aim for efficient management."},answer:"B",analysis:"Peretti 建议,面对当前形势,《纽约时报》应该____ 【判型】Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____ 直接询问 【拆句】Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____ 主句是 Peretti suggests that 引导的宾语从句，从句主语是 the Times，should 后接动词短语， 是待补全陈述句；in face of the present situation 是插入状语，限定建议的语境，结构平 【定位】P4 Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way. 【选项】A) 与原文相反 Peretti 的主张恰恰是 only if they go about doing it the right way，并明确警告 if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you；选项 end the print edition for good 把“讲方式地退出”极端化为“一刀切永 B) ✓ 正确 Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way ↔ make strategic adjustments I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product ↔ make strategic adjustments 预判 'the Times 应在节奏上加速、在路径上讲究方式' 完全对应 make strategic 读者来源，seek new sources of readership 在原文里没有任何对应表述。 打造 legacy product），并未谈到管理是否高效；aim for efficient management 把",position:0},{id:38,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:'It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a "legacy product" ____',options:{A:"helps restore the glory of former times.",B:"is meant for the most loyal customers.",C:"will have the cost of printing reduced.",D:"expands the popularity of the paper."},answer:"B",analysis:`【判型】It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a "legacy product"____ 用 inferred 这 【拆句】It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a "legacy product"____ 用 it 作形式主 语，真主语是 that 引导的从句；从句主语 a "legacy product" 后跟选项补全谓语； inferred from … that … 是固定结构，提示“根据……可推出……”。 【定位】P6 The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in. … In other words, if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it. 【选项】A) 过度推断 日辉煌”这种怀旧叙事；helps restore the glory of former times 是借 legacy 一词的 B) ✓ 正确 The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor ↔ is meant for the most loyal customers if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it ↔ is meant for the most loyal customers 选项 is meant for the most loyal customers 就是预判语义的最简短表述：legacy P5 与 P6 都在谈 raise prices、higher rate each year、generate additional revenue，全是涨收入侧；从未提到印刷成本会被降低，will have the cost of printing reduced 与文意走反方向。 Peretti 的方案是把产品收窄给 the people who are already obsessed with it，明显属 于受众收敛策略；expands the popularity of the paper 把方向反成“扩大受众/影响`,position:0},{id:39,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"Peretti believes that, in a changing world, ____",options:{A:"traditional luxuries can stay unaffected.",B:"cautiousness facilitates problem-solving.",C:"aggressiveness better meets challenges.",D:"legacy businesses are becoming outdated."},answer:"C",analysis:"Peretti 认为,在一个变化的世界中,____ 【判型】Peretti believes that, in a changing world,____ 问 Peretti 的明确信念，且原文末段会出 【拆句】Peretti believes that, in a changing world,____ 是 Peretti believes that 引导的宾语从 句，in a changing world 为插入状语，从句主谓宾由选项补全；结构清晰、无陷阱。 【定位】P7 But we're going to have questions like that where we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes. In those situations, it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive. 【选项】A) 偷换概念 it's a tremendous luxury that BuzzFeed doesn't have a legacy business 中 luxury 比喻“BuzzFeed 没历史包袱是种巨大幸运”，与“传统奢侈品”毫无关系；traditional luxuries can stay unaffected 把比喻义中的 luxury 死板字面化，并加上“不受影响”这 Peretti 明确说 it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive，与 cautiousness facilitates problem-solving 主张的“谨慎有助解决问题”正好相反。 C) ✓ 正确 it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive ↔ aggressiveness better meets challenges we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes ↔ aggressiveness better meets challenges 预判语义是“更激进胜过更保守”，唯一匹配的选项就是 aggressiveness better meets challenges，连关键词 aggressive 都被原词保留。 言“legacy businesses 正在过时”这一总论断；legacy businesses are becoming",position:0},{id:40,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:`Which of the following would be the best title of the text? Part B Directions: Read the following text and answer the questions by choosing the most suitable subheading from the list A-G for each of the numbered paragraphs (41-45). There are two extra subheadings. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points) No matter how formal or informal the work environment, the way you present yourself has an impact. This is especially true in first impressions. According to research from Princeton University, people assess your competence, trustworthiness, and likeability in just a tenth of a second, solely based on the way you look. The difference between today's workplace and the "dress for success" era is that the range of options is so much broader. Norms have evolved and fragmented. In some settings, red sneakers or dress T-shirts can convey status; in others not so much. Plus, whatever image we present is magnified by social-media services like LinkedIn. Chances are, your headshots are seen much more often now than a decade or two ago. Millennials, it seems, face the paradox of being the least formal generation yet the most conscious of style and personal branding. It can be confusing. So how do we navigate this? How do we know when to invest in an upgrade? And what's the best way to pull off one that enhances our goals? Here are some tips: (41)占位符这是等待完型填空的句⼦位置 As an executive coach, I've seen image upgrades be particularly helpful during transitions – when looking for a new job, stepping into a new or more public role, or changing work environments. If you're in a period of change or just feeling stuck and in a rut, now may be a good time. If you're not sure, ask for honest feedback from trusted friends, colleagues and professionals. Look for cues about how others perceive you. Maybe there's no need for an upgrade and that's OK. (42)占位符这是等待完型填空的句⼦位置 Get clear on what impact you're hoping to have. Are you looking to refresh your image or pivot it? For one person, the goal may be to be taken more seriously and enhance their professional image. For another, it may be to be perceived as more approachable, or more modern and stylish. For someone moving from finance to advertising, maybe they want to look more "SoHo." (It's OK to use characterizations like that.) (43)占位符这是等待完型填空的句⼦位置 Look at your work environment like an anthropologist. What are the norms of your environment? What conveys status? Who are your most important audiences? How do the people you respect and look up to present themselves? The better you understand the cultural context, the more control you can have over your impact. (44)占位符这是等待完型填空的句⼦位置 Enlist the support of professionals and share with them your goals and context. Hire a personal stylist, or use the free styling service of a store like J.Crew. Try a hair stylist instead of a barber. Work with a professional photographer instead of your spouse or friend. It's not as expensive as you might think. (45)占位符这是等待完型填空的句⼦位置 The point of a style upgrade isn't to become more vain or to spend more time fussing over what to wear. Instead, use it as an opportunity to reduce decision fatigue. Pick a standard work uniform or a few go-to options. Buy all your clothes at once with a stylist instead of shopping alone, one article of clothing at a time. [ E ]Work with professionals [ F ]Know your goals [ G ]Make it efficient Part C Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points) Mental health is our birthright. (46)We don't have to learn how to be mentally healthy; it is built into us in the same way that our bodies know how to heal a cut or mend a broken bone. Mental health can't be learned, only reawakened. It is like the immune system of the body, which under stress or through lack of nutrition or exercise can be weakened, but which never leaves us. When we don't understand the value of mental health and we don't know how to gain access to it, mental health will remain hidden from us. (47)Our mental health doesn't really go anywhere; like the sun behind a cloud, it can be temporarily hidden from view, but it is fully capable of being restored in an instant. Mental health is the seed that contains self-esteem – confidence in ourselves and an ability to trust in our common sense. It allows us to have perspective on our lives – the ability to not take ourselves too seriously, to laugh at ourselves, to see the bigger picture, and to see that things will work out. It's a form of innate or unlearned optimism. (48)Mental health allows us to view others with sympathy if they are having troubles, with kindness if they are in pain, and with unconditional love no matter who they are. Mental health is the source of creativity for solving problems, resolving conflict, making our surroundings more beautiful, managing our home life, or coming up with a creative business idea or invention to make our lives easier. It gives us patience for ourselves and toward others as well as patience while driving, catching a fish, working on our car, or raising a child. It allows us to see the beauty that surrounds us each moment in nature, in culture, in the flow of our daily lives. (49)Although mental health is the cure-all for living our lives, it is perfectly ordinary as you will see that it has been there to direct you through all your difficult decisions. It has been available even in the most mundane of life situations to show you right from wrong, good from bad, friend from foe. Mental health has commonly been called conscience, instinct, wisdom, common sense, or the inner voice. We think of it simply as a healthy and helpful flow of intelligent thought. (50)As you will come to see, knowing that mental health is always available and knowing to trust it allows us to slow down to the moment and live life happily.`,options:{A:"Create a new image of yourself",B:"Have confidence in yourself",C:"Decide if the time is right",D:"Understand the context"},answer:"B",analysis:"【判型】Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 显式问全文最佳标题，要求 【拆句】Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 是 which 引导的特殊疑问 【选项】A) 与原文相反 原文核心主张恰恰是 rushing to eliminate its print edition would be a mistake 与 if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you，明确反对一夜全转线上；Shift to Online Newspapers All at Once 把转折 B) ✓ 正确 I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product ↔ Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good Getting the print edition seven days a week costs nearly $500 a year – more than twice as much as a digital-only subscription ↔ Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it ↔ Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good 原文承认 the Times 终将停掉纸版，只是建议在过渡期把纸版打造成 legacy product； Keep Your Newspapers Forever in Fashion 中 Forever in Fashion 把方案绝对化、永 Cherish the Newspaper Still in Your Hand 只是一句情感号召，呼吁读者珍惜手中报 纸，没有体现“涨价 + 做成 legacy product + 面向忠实读者”等任何核心主张，仅与 The most loyal customers 的局部情感色彩沾边。 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 13 There will eventually come a day when The New York Times ceases to publish stories on newsprint. Nostalgia for ink on paper and the rustle of pages aside, there's plenty of incentive to ditch print. Readers are migrating away from print anyway. And though print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts, revenue from print is still declining. Peretti says the Times shouldn't wast...",position:0}]}],n={id:e,year:2016,subject:t,title:a,sections:o};export{n as default,e as id,o as sections,t as subject,a as title,i as year};
